# Encoding 2: the exception for Opus written against the rule itself - a
# counter-instance refutes forall x, Bird x -> Flies x (AIDA's decision Q4:
# a general rule stands or falls as one statement). Opus then brings the
# rule down for Tweety too, which no system that instantiates schemas per
# individual does (ASPIC+, DeLP, defeasible logic, s(CASP)).
lk.
declare Animal : type.
declare tweety, opus : Animal.
declare Bird, Penguin, Flies : Animal -> bool.
declare bird_tweety : (Bird [tweety]).
declare bird_opus : (Bird [opus]).
declare opus_grounded : (Flies [opus] -> false).
argument flies_tweety : (Flies [tweety]).
cut (forall x:Animal, Bird [x] -> Flies [x]) r.
by default.
next.
elim [tweety].
elim.
axiom bird_tweety.
axiom r.
dixi.
counterargument rule_fails : (forall x:Animal, Bird [x] -> Flies [x]).
elim [opus].
elim.
axiom bird_opus.
cut (Flies [opus] -> false) g.
axiom opus_grounded.
elim g.
axiom.
elim.
dixi.
